souran (5.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Security: purged a plaintext sudo password that was embedded in six
    source files and had already reached git history. Every call site now
    uses sudo -n.
  * Security: token authentication on the whole control plane. A
    root-or-service-owned 0600 token lives outside the source tree, is
    compared in constant time, and is required for every control route
    except health and docs. Loopback stays exempt so the watchdog and test
    suites keep working.
  * Security: host firewall. INPUT policy drop, OUTPUT deliberately
    unfiltered because an egress policy would break censorship bypass by
    construction. The NAT table is never flushed -- it holds the outbound
    DNS-to-Tor redirect the whole bypass stack depends on.
  * Security: poison detection now handles IPv6. It was IPv4-only via
    socket.inet_aton(), and the bare except swallowed the error, so every
    AAAA address was classified clean -- including this network's forged
    2001:4188:2:600:10:10:34:36, which is Telegram's real prefix with the
    censor's IPv4 answer written into it as decimal groups.
  * Security: the firewall no longer opens SSH and both dashboards to
    every source on every interface, and the DHCP rule is no longer a
    spoofable source-port match.
  * Fix: NXDOMAIN was being destroyed. All three handlers rebuilt the
    reply flags from scratch, zeroing the RCODE, so every NXDOMAIN reached
    clients as NOERROR. A DoH NXDOMAIN was also treated as a lookup
    failure, so the client was handed SERVFAIL instead.
  * Fix: a malformed query produced NO reply at all, hanging clients for
    their full timeout. Now an immediate FORMERR, including on the path
    where the error builder itself raised on the over-long label.
  * Fix: the DoT certificate had no subjectAltName, so Android Private
    DNS, Windows DNS-over-HTTPS and macOS could not use encrypted DNS at
    all. Replaced with a local root CA plus a leaf carrying DNS and IP
    SANs, and DoTServer no longer builds a fresh SSLContext per accept.
  * Fix: the watchdog issued 6 repair calls against a dns.service that
    does not exist, logging 3,543 failures and sleeping as if it had
    worked. It now restarts the units that own the resolver.
  * Fix: the firewall was not owned by systemd and would have vanished on
    reboot, silently removing all access control.
  * Packaging: unbound is compiled from the vendored source during the
    build. TLS private keys and all config snapshots are excluded from the
    payload; the postinst generates fresh keys on the target.
  * New: unified feature registry, 31 individually switchable features
    with desired-vs-probed state and drift detection, exposed through a
    control dashboard on :8082.
  * New: cross-platform client for Windows, macOS, Linux and Android.

 -- Hermes Agent <souran@sitet.top>  Sat, 04 Oct 2026 23:55:00 +0100

souran (5.0.0) resolute; urgency=low

  * Security: removed a plaintext sudo password that was embedded in six
    source files and had already reached git history. Every call site now
    uses sudo -n; the credential bought nothing because every unit runs
    unprivileged.
  * Security: added token authentication to the whole control plane. A
    root-or-service-owned 0600 token is stored outside the source tree,
    compared in constant time, and required for every control API route
    except the health and docs paths. Loopback callers stay exempt so the
    watchdog and test suites keep working.
  * Packaging: first release as a .deb. unbound is compiled from the
    vendored source during the build, so the shipped resolver is built
    from source on the target rather than copied in as a binary.
  * Packaging: TLS private keys and all *.bak / pre-* config snapshots are
    excluded from the payload. A distributable package must not ship the
    host's live private keys.

 -- Hermes Agent <souran@sitet.top>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 20:10:00 +0100

souran (4.3.6) resolute; urgency=low

  * Fixed the ground-truth oracle so MX and TXT answers are really
    verified rather than assumed.
  * Fixed truncated TXT replies corrupting the question section.
  * Added a systemd unit for the ops sidecar; 19 API routes had been dead.

